  "critical": true,
  "description": "Electrochemical energy storage. Lead-acid battery (Plante 1859): Pb anode, PbO2 cathode, 37% H2SO4 electrolyte, 2.0 V/cell nominal, 30-50 Wh/kg, robust and recyclable (>95% lead recovery). Nickel-iron (Edison): 1.2 V/cell, survives deep discharge. Later lithium-ion: graphite anode, layered metal-oxide cathode (LiCoO2, LiFePO4), non-aqueous electrolyte, 3.6 V/cell, 150-250 Wh/kg. Enables off-grid power, telecom backup, vehicle starting, and portable electronics.",
